:name: windmeter peripheral-stimulus proof
:Loads the real compiled firmware ELF onto an emulated STM32H723ZG and
:drives its GPIO/ADC/UART/CAN peripherals with synthetic stimulus,
:proving the firmware's actual embedded driver code reacts correctly --
:not the host-side logic Task 6's `simulate` binary already covers, but
:the GPIO/ADC/UART/FDCAN peripheral code paths simulation can't reach.
:See PROJECT_PRINCIPLES.md for what's actually confirmed vs. attempted.
:This is a complement to, not a replacement for, tasks.md's 1a/2a/5a:
:those need real hardware/a real antenna/a real N2K bus, which no
:emulator can substitute for -- this only proves the driver code, not
:the physical sensors or bus.
:
:CAN: fully working -- fdcan1 is connected to a hub and every
:transmitted frame is logged, confirming real PGN 130306 bytes leaving
:the real FDCAN1 peripheral driver.
:
:GPIO (anemometer pulses)/UART (GPS sentences): the injection calls
:below (`gpioPortA OnGPIO`/`usart3 WriteLine`) demonstrably change the
:right hardware state (confirmed separately by reading IDR/ISR back),
:but the firmware never reacts -- EXTI0's handler is never entered and
:USART3's RXNE never sets, even with NVIC/EXTI/RTSR1/IMR1 all correctly
:configured. This looks like a gap in how this Renode peripheral-model
:combination propagates externally-injected stimulus through to
:STM32-specific interrupt/DMA machinery, not a firmware bug or a wiring
:mistake on this script's part -- left in as working groundwork (the
:monitor-level mechanics are right) for whoever picks this up next.
:
:Rebuild first: `cargo build --target thumbv7em-none-eabihf`
:Run from Renode's own install dir (the `using`/`i @platforms/...`
:paths below resolve relative to it), pointing at this script, e.g.:
:   /path/to/renode --disable-gui --console \
:     -e 'i @/path/to/windmeter/renode/boot.resc' -e quit
:
:Output: /tmp/windmeter_rtt.bin (the firmware's own RTT log, decode with
:`defmt-print -e target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/debug/wind_meter <
:/tmp/windmeter_rtt.bin`) and /tmp/windmeter_can.log (one line per real
:NMEA2000 frame the firmware transmitted, id + raw bytes).

$bin ?= @/home/qarol/git/windmeter/windmeter/target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/debug/wind_meter

mach create "windmeter"
i @/home/qarol/git/windmeter/windmeter/renode/stm32h723zg.repl

cpu VectorTableOffset 0x8000000

# Renode's STM32H7_RCC model doesn't persist every bit this firmware's
# clock-mux setup writes (logged as "Unhandled bits" warnings -- a
# Renode-side gap, not a firmware bug: confirmed by reading each
# register back and seeing the dropped bits simply never stuck,
# regardless of what was written). Force reads of the two affected
# registers to return exactly what the firmware's own (correct) writes
# intended, captured from those warnings' logged write values: D3CCIPR
# (ADC1's mux) and D2CCIP1R (SPI1's and FDCAN1's).
rcc AddBeforeReadDoubleWordHook 0x58 "value = 0x20000"
rcc AddBeforeReadDoubleWordHook 0x50 "value = 0x10004000"

# Observe what actually goes out on the CAN bus -- fdcan1 is real
# firmware-driven silicon-level behavior, not a stand-in.
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"
connector Connect fdcan1 canHub

sysbus LoadELF $bin

i @/home/qarol/git/windmeter/windmeter/renode/fault_probe.py

# panic-probe traps into a debugger breakpoint on panic; with none
# attached, Renode sees it as an undefined-instruction fault. Hook
# HardFault's real address (resolved from the loaded ELF, since it
# shifts on every rebuild) so a panic's exception frame -- and thus the
# faulting PC -- is captured instead of silently free-running past it.
probe_hard_fault `sysbus GetSymbolAddress "HardFault_"`

probe_can fdcan1 "/tmp/windmeter_can.log"

# `_SEGGER_RTT`'s aUp[0] channel fields, relative to its own address
# (16-byte "SEGGER RTT" magic, MaxNumUpBuffers, MaxNumDownBuffers, then
# the aUp[] array): +0x1C pBuffer, +0x20 SizeOfBuffer, +0x24 WrOff,
# +0x28 RdOff. drain_rtt reads only what's new since its last call and
# advances RdOff, so calling it repeatedly across short RunFor hops
# (below) builds a lossless transcript -- a single dump at the very end
# would lose early events to the ring buffer wrapping under a chatty
# peripheral (the SD-card driver retries hard with no real card
# present).
$rtt_cb = `sysbus GetSymbolAddress "_SEGGER_RTT"`

# Let firmware init reach the point where PA0/EXTI0 and ADC1 are
# actually configured (well under 1ms of virtual time -- "ADC frequency
# set" logs at ~125us) before driving them; then inject stimulus inside
# wind_sensor_task's *first* 1s sampling window, since logger_task's
# first tick (see below) blocks the whole single-threaded executor for
# several virtual seconds retrying a card that isn't there (real
# embedded-sdmmc behavior, not a Renode artifact: `AcquireOpts {
# retries: 50 }` against an SPI1 that never answers) -- this first
# window, before that tick lands, is the only reliably live one.
emulation RunFor "0.5"

# Wind vane direction (PA1 / ADC1 channel 17, see
# WindCalibration::davis_6410_defaults' adc_max=4095 and Vref=3.3V):
# ~1650mV should land near mid-scale, i.e. ~180 degrees.
adcM1S2 SetVoltage 1650 17

# Anemometer pulses (PA0/EXTI0, rising-edge counted): 5 pulses inside
# wind_sensor_task's first 1s sampling window, driven directly via
# gpioPortA's OnGPIO (the same call an external IRQ source -- e.g. a
# Miscellaneous.Button -- would make; going straight to it sidesteps a
# Button-via-repl wiring that didn't actually move gpioPortA's IDR in
# testing). mps_per_hz ~1.006 (davis_6410_defaults) -> ~5.03 m/s
# expected.
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 True
emulation RunFor "0.02"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 False
emulation RunFor "0.1"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 True
emulation RunFor "0.02"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 False
emulation RunFor "0.1"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 True
emulation RunFor "0.02"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 False
emulation RunFor "0.1"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 True
emulation RunFor "0.02"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 False
emulation RunFor "0.1"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 True
emulation RunFor "0.02"
gpioPortA OnGPIO 0 False
emulation RunFor "0.1"

# A real NMEA0183 RMC sentence (SOG 5.50 kn, COG 90 deg), the exact
# fixture already proven correct in gps.rs's own unit tests -- fed a
# character at a time at USART3's actual configured 9600 baud, same as
# a real NEO-6M would.
usart3 WriteLine "$GPRMC,125504.049,A,5542.2389,N,03741.6063,E,5.50,90.00,200906,,,A*54" false

drain_rtt $rtt_cb "/tmp/windmeter_rtt.bin"
echo "--- drained after stimulus, before RunFor 1 ---"

emulation RunFor "1"
drain_rtt $rtt_cb "/tmp/windmeter_rtt.bin"

emulation RunFor "2"
drain_rtt $rtt_cb "/tmp/windmeter_rtt.bin"

echo "=== CPU state ==="
sysbus.cpu PC
sysbus.cpu IsHalted
echo "RTT transcript -> /tmp/windmeter_rtt.bin, CAN frames -> /tmp/windmeter_can.log"
